{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HrqythBhBHHVvVid4Apjxa","type":"tool_result","content":"<!-- nightralph:start -->\n## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues are tracked as local markdown files under `.scratch/`. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Triage labels\n\nDefault label vocabulary. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\nSingle-context layout. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.\n\n### Button attribute forwarding\n\n`FORWARDED_ATTRS` in `src/client.ts` drives both dynamic host-attribute\nmirroring and attributes supplied to the full renderer. A new forwarded\nattribute must also pass through `HANDLED_KEYS` in `src/html.ts`.\n\nAn attribute that needs its own semantics (`class`, `aria-label`) gets a\n`handleChange_<name>` method instead; any such handler suppresses generic\nforwarding in `attributeChangedCallback`. Hydration of an app-rendered\nbutton happens in the light element's `connectedCallback`.\n\nTest forwarding at the public custom-element seam with\n`esbuild test/index.ts --bundle | tapout`; cover both a rendered button and\nthe app-rendered hydration path when applicable.\n<!-- nightralph:end -->\n3:  \"version\": \"0.0.55\",\n36:    \"lint\": \"eslint \\\"./**/*.{ts,js}\\\"\",\n37:    \"test\": \"node test/package-version.js && npm run build && esbuild test/index.ts --bundle | tapout\",\n51:    \"version\": \"npm run toc && auto-changelog -p --template keepachangelog --breaking-pattern 'BREAKING CHANGE:' && git add CHANGELOG.md README.md\",\n86:    \"test\": \"test\"\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict'\nimport { readFile } from 'node:fs/promises'\n\nconst manifestUrl = new URL('../package.json', import.meta.url)\nconst manifest = JSON.parse(await readFile(manifestUrl, 'utf8'))\n\nassert.equal(\n    manifest.version,\n    '0.0.55',\n    'the next release after v0.0.54 uses version 0.0.55'\n)\n# Changelog\n\nAll notable changes to this project will be documented in this file.\n\nThe format is based on [Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/en/1.0.0/)\nand this project adheres to [Semantic Versioning](https://semver.org/spec/v2.0.0.html).\n\nGenerated by [`auto-changelog`](https://github.com/CookPete/auto-changelog).\n\n## [v0.0.54](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.53...v0.0.54)\n\n### Commits\n\n- fix from knitting party [`b7ba934`](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/commit/b7ba934fd51842a9707d9fd5c97dee537eecb1e5)\n\n## [v0.0.53](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.52...v0.0.53) - 2026-10-15\n\n## [v0.0.52](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.51...v0.0.52) - 2026-10-03\n\n## [v0.0.51](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.50...v0.0.51) - 2026-10-03\n\n## [v0.0.50](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.49...v0.0.50) - 2026-10-03\n\n### Commits\n\n- add ticket [`6d53d14`](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/commit/6d53d146803d8b7dd9aa62901f5e1a9486d011e7)\n- fix bug [`9007d10`](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/commit/9007d1085874ae56441e7024ef2966b8ecbab7e8)\n\n## [v0.0.49](https://github.com/substrate-system/button/compare/v0.0.48...v0.0.49) - 2026-06-29\n\n53:The CSS reads these variables. They are shared with the other\n167:  classes: ['abc'],\n185:  <button class=\"substrate-button btn\" type=\"submit\">\n186:    <span class=\"btn-content\">Save</span>\n194:`btn` classes match what the element renders itself, and are\n233:<substrate-button id=\"labeled\" aria-label=\"Save your changes\">\n245:`popovertarget`, `popovertargetaction`, `title`, and `aria-live`.\n247:Set `aria-live` on the `<substrate-button>` host only when your app needs\n250:The host's `class` also follows onto the inner button, including a button\n251:rendered by your app before the element hydrates. Classes you add to the host\n252:are added to the inner button, and classes you remove are removed from it.\n253:The classes the element owns, `substrate-button`, `btn`, and `spinning`, are\n254:never added or removed by a host class change.\n255:On a button rendered by your app, the app owns the button's `class`. If the\n256:app changes that attribute, include any host classes it wants kept. If the\n257:app replaces its button, the new button does not receive the host class or\n263:`aria-disabled`, and native `disabled` is the source of truth.\n265:`ariaLabel` names the inner button, and the host never carries an\n266:`aria-label`. A host `aria-label` attribute moves onto the inner button,\n267:and a later `setAttribute('aria-label', ...)` also moves. The element keeps\n268:it off the host, because `aria-label` on an element with no role fails axe.\n269:Reading `el.ariaLabel` returns the inner button's label. Removing the host\n271:label, set `el.ariaLabel = null`. In Preact or another framework, pass\n272:`ariaLabel` as a property, not `aria-label` as an attribute. Removing the\n278:el.ariaLabel = 'Close the dialog'\n281:el.ariaLabel = ''\n284:`aria-live` is opt-in: set it on the `<substrate-button>` host when your app\n286:has `aria-busy=\"true\"`.\n288:Upgrade note: if your app relied on the previous default `aria-live` value,\n289:set `aria-live` on the host to restore it.\n295:starts and ends. It may use the app's visually hidden class.\n299:<p id=\"save-status\" role=\"status\" class=\"visually-hidden\"></p>","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f6aec845-8048-4697-8a00-9a0538480568","uuid":"2e25070c-b74f-453d-8ddd-31e94bd998e6","timestamp":"2026-10-30T03:34:32.650Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"<!-- nightralph:start -->\n## Agent skills\n\n### Issue tracker\n\nIssues are tracked as local markdown files under `.scratch/`. See `docs/agents/issue-tracker.md`.\n\n### Triage labels\n\nDefault label vocabulary. See `docs/agents/triage-labels.md`.\n\n### Domain docs\n\nSingle-context layout. See `docs/agents/domain.md`.\n\n### Button attribute forwarding\n\n`FORWARDED_ATTRS` in `src/c